WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.790
What do you need to know before you jump into
the MIB's next chapter? How will Chris Hemsworth

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.810
and Tessa Thompson take to the black suits?
Will we get to see Will Smith and Tommy Lee

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:12.599
Jones rock the Ray Bans in this one? We've
got a primer to get you ready for Men in Black:

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.300
International.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.920
Based on what we can gather from the trailers,
it appears that Tessa Thompson's character

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.500
is Agent M, a new recruit sent to partner
alongside Chris Hemsworth's Agent H to crack

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.099
a murder mystery and prevent a new alien threat.
Thompson's character seems to get her start

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:31.010
with the Men In Black by discovering their
New York City headquarters before being dispatched

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.880
to the organization's London outpost.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.580
Although the film is international, it's important
that the movie begins in NYC. After all, the

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.690
city was essentially a main character in the
original film. Barry Sonnenfeld, director

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:45.550
of Men in Black, made sure that the movie
was set in the Big Apple, as part of a joke

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.500
that New Yorkers would barely notice alien
life living among them.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:53.280
In the first movie, Agent K tells Agent J
that the MIB in New York was created right

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.400
before alien visitors arrived on our planet
just outside New York in the sixties.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.300
"Everyone thought the agency was a joke except
the aliens who made contact March 2, 1961

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.340
outside New York."

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.440
However, the upcoming movie takes place all
over the world, with the production shooting

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.720
in England, Morocco, and Italy. These are
countries that are obviously far older than

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.720
the United States, and may reveal a deeper
history of aliens on planet Earth than the

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.080
earlier movies let on.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.920
When word got out Men in Black: International
was on the way, the big question on everyone's

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:25.920
mind was whether we would see Will Smith and
Tommy Lee Jones back in the saddle. In the

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.680
film's trailer, fans are treated to a J and
K Easter egg. A painting on the wall depicts

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.730
Smith's Agent J and Jones' Agent K fighting
the insectoid alien from the first movie.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.560
But will the characters themselves make a
cameo in the new film? The initial word was

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.740
that Smith and Jones would not participate.
Since then, however, some comments from director

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.980
F. Gary Gray have led to speculation that
we could see a cameo from the original duo.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.160
All we can do is hope.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.260
Gray is directing International from a screenplay
by Matt Holloway and Art Marcum, the duo who

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:59.510
wrote 2008's Iron Man. Steven Spielberg is
back as executive producer, the role he served

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:03.700
on the original trilogy. Besides Hemsworth
and Thompson, Liam Neeson will play the head

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.500
of MIB London, though it's unclear how much
screen time the character will get.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:11.500
The spin-off has a strong supporting cast
as well. Emma Thompson will reprise her role

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:17.010
from Men in Black III as Agent O. Kumail Nanjiani
is playing a comedic alien sidekick, and Rebecca

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.960
Ferguson has signed on as a lead, likely as
a villain battling Hemsworth and Thompson.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:25.920
The original films were beloved not just for
being fantastic adventures with out-of-this-world

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.270
aliens and technology, but also for their
humor.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.500
"At first I was gonna pop this guy hanging
from the streetlight, but then I realized

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.590
that he's just working out. How would I feel
if I'm running in the gym someone busts in

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:35.880
and caps my ass while I'm on the treadmill?"

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.970
In addition to Will Smith's gift for physical
comedy and Tommy Lee Jones' patented deadpan,

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:45.640
the films also succeed as satire, making keen
insights about race and immigration. After

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:50.360
all, the first movie is about alien visitation
by intergalactic refugees seeking asylum.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.610
Given today's political climate, you can look
back at Men in Black as a progressive parable

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:59.620
about taking a compassionate approach to immigration
policies. Tessa Thompson certainly does, telling

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:00.200
EW:

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.180
"I mean, the start of the first movie talks
about immigration, and Will [Smith] has these

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.989
really searing jokes about race…I think
you do have the chance inside of all this

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:09.440
escapism to say something."

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.480
Men in Black: International further solidifies
the franchise's comedy chops with director

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:17.870
F. Gary Gray, who directed the comedy classic
Friday. On the acting side of things, Kumail

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:22.349
Nanjiani, known for The Big Sick and Silicon
Valley, is sure to bring laughs. Still, we

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:26.550
can't forget Chris Hemsworth. It's easy to
only imagine Hemsworth as the God of Thunder,

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:31.520
but with brilliant turns in Ghostbusters,
Vacation, and SNL, Hemsworth is building quite

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.090
the comedic resume. Tessa Thompson is no slouch
in the comedy department either. Considering

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.350
the hilarious moments she shared with Hemsworth
in Thor: Ragnarok, it's no surprise that fans

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.080
are excited to see the pair reteam to don
the black suits.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.300
The International trailer hints at more of
the cool weapons and technology that have

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.160
become a hallmark of the Men in Black series.
In one clip, fans are treated to an array

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.319
of secret weapons revealing themselves from
within a sleek black car. In addition to the

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:59.720
futuristic laser guns, the trailer also provides
a decidedly lighthearted low-tech moment,

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.740
in which Agent H throws a hammer at an alien
adversary.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.580
"Looks like the tables have turned."

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.000
"That was an incredible catch."

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.020
It's certainly not the first time one of Hemsworth's
hammer tosses didn't go according to plan:

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.000
"I don't think so."

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:25.979
The trailer also features the most iconic
MIB gadget of all: the neuralyzer. Ironically,

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:30.259
one of the most memorable aspects of the original
Men in Black was this memory-erasing device

00:04:30.259 --> 00:04:34.300
used to make witnesses forget everything about
agents and alien lifeforms. The inclusion

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.370
of the neuralyzer in the trailer is a nice
nostalgic touch and basically a necessity

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.000
for any MIB sequel.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.879
And then there's the franchise's signature
look.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.900
"You know what the difference is between you
and me?"

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.680
"I make this look good."

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.139
That iconic scene defined a big aspect of
the series' appeal: the style. If the trailers

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:59.150
are anything to go by, the names might have
changed, but the effortlessly cool minimalist

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.590
look hasn't gone anywhere.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:04.949
The sleek cars are also a crucial part of
the MIB series, and it looks like International

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:09.470
won't disappoint on that end. In London, we
see the aforementioned spy-car with secret

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:14.870
weapon racks, a 1970s Jaguar XJ. Later in
the trailer, we also see Hemsworth and Thompson

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:20.300
riding in a Lexus RC F sports car. In a nod
to the 1980s Ford LTD Crown Victoria in the

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:24.040
first movie, the RC F can also fly at the
press of a big red button.

